  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **The House That Dripped Blood** (1 review): Darnielle's banter at the song's end mentions he had not previously played the next song electric [3]\n- **You or Your Memory** (1 review): Reviewer is faintly audible at the end saying it works on electric; Darnielle had never played it electric before [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Peacocks**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [6]\n- **The House That Dripped Blood**: rare: 7 archived performances [6]\n- **Half Dead**: rare: 9 archived performances [6]\n- **The Boys Are Back In Town**: rare: 5 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2007-03-08** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 80 min; rated 5/5 by 4 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- John Vanderslice joined the band on stage, standing at the corner where the reviewer was positioned [3]\n- Jon Wurster of Superchunk played drums, and the reviewer thought the band never sounded better [4]\n- The 03/07/2007 show sounds equally good but has noisy drunk audience members; Darnielle seems to enjoy this night more [2]\n- Setlists of this show and the 03/07 show are very similar, so the reviewer favors this one [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2007-03-08**: taped by Chris Bellew; transferred by Chris Bellew; source: SP-CMC-2>SP-SPSB-1>iRiver ihp-140 [1]. Also: Reviewer taped from the audience but lost the main set data when changing batteries before the encores; only encores survived [4]",
